---
import Public from "../layouts/Public.astro";
---

<Public title="Home" description="See where your AI agent spend and latency go with session-level flame telemetry.">
  <style>
    .hero {
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 1.2rem;
      padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 14% 10%, rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.2), transparent 34%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 88% 18%, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.22), transparent 36%),
        var(--pub-surface);
      margin-top: 0.2rem;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.35rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 0.28rem 0.56rem;
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--pub-accent);
      background: rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.14);
    }

    .title {
      margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
      font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 7vw, 3.4rem);
      line-height: 1.03;
      max-width: 18ch;
    }

    .subtitle {
      color: var(--pub-text-subtle);
      max-width: 58ch;
      margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.55rem;
    }

    .hero-btn {
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.87rem;
      padding: 0.6rem 0.95rem;
      border: 1px solid transparent;
    }

    .hero-btn.primary {
      background: var(--pub-accent);
      color: #fff;
    }

    .hero-btn.primary:hover {
      background: var(--pub-accent-strong);
    }

    .hero-btn.secondary {
      background: var(--pub-surface-2);
      border-color: var(--pub-border);
      color: var(--pub-text);
    }

    .hero-btn.secondary:hover {
      border-color: var(--pub-accent);
      color: var(--pub-accent);
    }

    .telemetry-card {
      margin-top: 1.2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.9rem;
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
      padding: 0.9rem;
    }

    .telemetry-head {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--pub-text-dim);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .lanes {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.32rem;
      align-items: end;
      min-height: 7.6rem;
      padding: 0.45rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--pub-surface-2);
    }

    .bar {
      border-radius: 0.3rem;
      animation: rise 3s ease-in-out infinite;
      position: relative;
    }

    .bar:nth-child(4n) { background: #7c3aed; }
    .bar:nth-child(4n+1) { background: #f59e0b; }
    .bar:nth-child(4n+2) { background: #06b6d4; }
    .bar:nth-child(4n+3) { background: #ef4444; }

    @keyframes rise {
      0%, 100% { transform: scaleY(0.68); }
      50% { transform: scaleY(1); }
    }

    .stats {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.7rem;
      margin-top: 0.85rem;
    }

    .stat {
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.7rem;
      padding: 0.68rem;
      background: var(--pub-surface);
    }

    .stat-k {
      color: var(--pub-text-dim);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      font-size: 0.69rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .stat-v {
      margin-top: 0.3rem;
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 1.08rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .section {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--pub-surface);
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .section h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 1.8rem);
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .section p {
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
      color: var(--pub-text-subtle);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .problem-grid {
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.65rem;
    }

    .problem {
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.82rem;
      background: var(--pub-surface-2);
    }

    .problem strong {
      display: block;
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: var(--pub-accent);
    }

    .problem span {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--pub-text-subtle);
      line-height: 1.5;
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.3rem;
    }

    .features {
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.65rem;
    }

    .feature {
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.82rem;
      background: var(--pub-surface-2);
    }

    .feature-id {
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
      color: var(--pub-accent);
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .feature h3 {
      margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .feature p {
      margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--pub-text-subtle);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .code {
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
      background: #0b1325;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .code-head {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 0.55rem 0.72rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);
      color: #b5c5e5;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .copy-btn {
      border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);
      border-radius: 0.45rem;
      background: transparent;
      color: #d1def6;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .copy-btn:hover {
      border-color: #f97316;
      color: #f97316;
    }

    .code pre {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0.85rem;
      overflow: auto;
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
      color: #d9e5ff;
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .cta {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--pub-border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      padding: 1.2rem;
      text-align: center;
      background: linear-gradient(140deg, rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.18), rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.14));
    }

    .cta h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 1.9rem);
    }

    .cta p {
      margin: 0.55rem auto 0;
      color: var(--pub-text-subtle);
      max-width: 54ch;
    }

    .cta a {
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
      display: inline-flex;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.7rem;
      background: var(--pub-accent);
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      padding: 0.62rem 1rem;
    }

    .cta a:hover {
      background: var(--pub-accent-strong);
    }

    @media (max-width: 920px) {
      .stats,
      .problem-grid,
      .features {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 660px) {
      .stats,
      .problem-grid,
      .features {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <section class="hero">
    <span class="badge">Public beta</span>
    <h1 class="title">Trace every token path your AI agent executes</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Token Flame Graph maps each call, tool run, and context rebuild into one session timeline so teams can cut spend and debug faster.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="hero-btn primary" href="/sign-up">Start free</a>
      <a class="hero-btn secondary" href="/docs">Read integration docs</a>
    </div>

    <div class="telemetry-card">
      <div class="telemetry-head">
        <span>live session telemetry</span>
        <span>cost alert active</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lanes">
        {Array.from({ length: 12 }).map((_, idx) => (
          <div class="bar" style={{ height: `${36 + (idx % 6) * 10}%`, animationDelay: `${idx * 0.08}s` }}></div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-k">Tokens</div>
          <div class="stat-v">47,832</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-k">Cost</div>
          <div class="stat-v">$0.86</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-k">Loops</div>
          <div class="stat-v">3</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Why teams use it</h2>
    <p>Production agent behavior is often opaque. This makes token burn visible and actionable in minutes.</p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <article class="problem">
        <strong>70%</strong>
        <span>of spend can hide in context bloat and retries without clear tracing.</span>
      </article>
      <article class="problem">
        <strong>0 alerts</strong>
        <span>in many stacks before loops spiral. We flag them directly in session view.</span>
      </article>
      <article class="problem">
        <strong>Slow triage</strong>
        <span>when cost data lacks feature-level attribution. This links spend to workflow.</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Three core workflows</h2>
    <p>Designed for observability, not vanity dashboards.</p>
    <div class="features">
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-id">01 trace</div>
        <h3>Session flame structure</h3>
        <p>Inspect every run as stacked spans by turn, tool, and model segments.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-id">02 detect</div>
        <h3>Loop and waste signals</h3>
        <p>Highlight repeated execution patterns and context-heavy calls instantly.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="feature-id">03 enforce</div>
        <h3>Budget controls</h3>
        <p>Set per-session, per-agent, or per-call limits with warning/block actions.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Integration in minutes</h2>
    <p>Publish events from your existing PI agent with one collector wrapper.</p>
    <div class="code">
      <div class="code-head">
        <span>agent.ts</span>
        <button class="copy-btn" id="copy-code">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre id="code-snippet">{`import { instrumentAgent, LocalCollector } from "flamegraph-sdk";

const collector = new LocalCollector({
  serverUrl: process.env.FLAMEGRAPH_URL,
  apiKey: process.env.FLAMEGRAPH_API_KEY,
});

instrumentAgent(agent, { collector });`}</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Stop shipping blind cost regressions</h2>
    <p>Wire session telemetry before your next release and track model spend by real runtime behavior.</p>
    <a href="/sign-up">Create workspace</a>
  </section>

  <script>
    const copyBtn = document.getElementById("copy-code");
    const codeSnippet = document.getElementById("code-snippet");
    copyBtn?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      if (!codeSnippet) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeSnippet.innerText);
        const initial = copyBtn.textContent;
        copyBtn.textContent = "Copied";
        setTimeout(() => {
          copyBtn.textContent = initial;
        }, 1400);
      } catch {
        copyBtn.textContent = "Failed";
        setTimeout(() => {
          copyBtn.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1400);
      }
    });
  </script>
</Public>
